        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nFor a wider support, 'mini.icons' [prefers 'nf-md'*' glyphs](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/473cdbff498ed120f1768c75ef65fa42859aa14f/doc/mini-icons.txt#L305-L306) if they are present. This is the case with ['css' filetype](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/473cdbff498ed120f1768c75ef65fa42859aa14f/lua/mini/icons.lua#L1103). Exceptions can be made, of course, but I don't think this is the case with CSS (at least yet). In the meantime, users can adjust that icon with usual 'mini.icons' customization approach.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned (maybe can be revisited after significant amount of time has passed for the new-ish icon to be widely available; maybe after 4.0.0 Nerd font release).",
